<title>USA: Legislative terms lengthened by N. Dakota voters.</title>
<headline>Legislative terms lengthened by N. Dakota voters.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in North Dakota apparently have approved a ballot measure to lengthen the term of state representatives to four years from two years, according to the state secretary of state's office.</p>
<p>The office, which is still waiting to compute vote tallies, also reported that a second measure that would reinstate the doctrine of sovereign immunity apparently failed.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
</text>
